{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["The reason for <b>כל אלמנה</b> (any widow): even if she is wealthy, a woman of property, for her tears are ever-present and her spirit is lowly. And He said, <b>אם ענה תענה אותו</b> (if you afflict him), referring to each individual among them; therefore it is written afterward, <b>והיו נשיכם אלמנות</b> (your wives shall be widows) — as punishment for the widow and her outcry — <b>ובניכם יתומים</b> (and your sons orphans) — for the outcry of the orphan. And our Sages did not enumerate this punishment among those liable to death by the hand of Heaven in the baraita of 'These are the ones [punished] by death' cited in Sanhedrin (83a). The reason is that this is not a death like the death of human beings by the hand of Heaven, of whom it is said: 'ומתו בו כי יחללהו' (Leviticus 22:9) and 'ולא תמותו' (Numbers 18:32); rather, He punished here that the enemy's sword or war will kill them — they will descend and perish without announcement, and their wives will be widows forever and their sons orphans forever."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:18:17.515697143Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}